2076..2150 Comment "/// Reading twice is reading once at the same state. The inner `get` is an"
2151..2221 Comment "/// instance of the rule\'s own left side through its pattern, and both"
2222..2293 Comment "/// reducts read once and continue at that state three times (#2116). A"
2294..2445 Comment "/// scope over this theory runs its subject normalised by the rule: `let a = /// st.get(); let b = st.get(); pure a + b` reads once, `let a = st.get();"
2446..2519 Comment "/// pure a + a` with `b` bound to `a` (`state-laws.gandr`\'s `readTwice`)."
